  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "The current best configuration is RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool at ~0.650 accuracy (config_005/006). The most important remaining uncertainty is whether adding the image modality via fusion can improve upon this strong RNA-only baseline. Although image-only performance is weak (0.208 with ResNet50), that does not preclude complementary signal in a fused setting. Config_030 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, ResNet50, concat) is the simplest multimodal extension of the best RNA-only configuration, changing only the addition of the image channel with the most straightforward fusion (concat). A positive result would open a new optimization axis (fusion strategy, image encoder); a negative or neutral result would confirm that the RNA-only multiprofile pipeline is near the achievable ceiling and redirect effort toward other levers. This is the highest-information experiment under the limited budget because it directly tests the single largest unexplored design dimension (modality combination) while holding all other variables at their empirically best settings."
}

